{#
  Manual targeted deletes for stale config nodes.

  Add a `delete ...` line here whenever a node needs to be removed from the
  router that the set-command partials won't naturally overwrite (e.g. renamed
  keys, removed features, old peer names, retired rules).

  Lines are sent in configure mode before any `set` commands, so the router
  arrives at a clean state before the desired config is applied.

  When a delete is no longer needed (confirmed absent on the router), remove
  the line so this file stays tidy.

  Examples:
    delete interfaces wireguard wg0 peer <old-pubkey>
    delete service snmp v3 user olduser
    delete firewall ipv4 name RETIRED-CHAIN
    delete nat destination rule 99
#}
